WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.543 --> 00:00:05.379
MARGAERY: Some Great Houses
call us upstarts, but the truth is

00:00:05.464 --> 00:00:09.467
that while the Starks and Lannisters fell
to the Targaryens in defeat,

00:00:09.551 --> 00:00:11.886
House Tyrell rose.

00:00:12.304 --> 00:00:13.721
For thousands of years,

00:00:13.805 --> 00:00:17.975
our family served as loyal stewards
to the kings of the Reach,

00:00:18.227 --> 00:00:21.604
until the last of their line
unwisely burned to death,

00:00:21.813 --> 00:00:24.232
resisting the Targaryen invaders.

00:00:24.942 --> 00:00:27.443
To save the Reach from a similar fate,

00:00:27.528 --> 00:00:31.781
we yielded the castle of Highgarden
to Aegon and his sisters.

00:00:32.366 --> 00:00:37.703
ln gratitude, the Targaryens gave House Tyrell
dominion over the Reach,

00:00:38.497 --> 00:00:43.084
and we became lords of the castle
in which, for generations, we had served.

00:00:44.253 --> 00:00:47.672
Under the Targaryen dynasty,
Westeros prospered.

00:00:48.423 --> 00:00:50.883
Gone were the petty wars of Seven Kingdoms

00:00:50.968 --> 00:00:54.554
and the endless thirst
for minor glories that drove them.

00:00:54.638 --> 00:00:59.016
The Westerlands enriched the realm,
the North guarded it,

00:00:59.101 --> 00:01:01.978
and the Reach and Riverlands fed it.

00:01:02.479 --> 00:01:05.273
This harmony is what
Robert Baratheon shattered

00:01:05.357 --> 00:01:08.276
with his rebellion against Aerys Targaryen.

00:01:08.443 --> 00:01:12.446
When the call to arms came, though,
we did not want to answer.

00:01:13.115 --> 00:01:14.657
The Reach is a gentle land,

00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:18.077
and, honestly,
the Mad King was not much loved.

00:01:18.829 --> 00:01:21.706
But we owed peace and status to his family.

00:01:22.165 --> 00:01:25.710
My father, Mace Tyrell, called his banners

00:01:25.794 --> 00:01:29.255
and marched north to battle
the rogue Storm Lord, Robert,

00:01:29.339 --> 00:01:33.134
who had already defeated
three forces in a single day.

00:01:33.677 --> 00:01:35.595
And, at Ashford,

00:01:36.555 --> 00:01:38.556
my father won.

00:01:39.099 --> 00:01:43.185
Some chasten my father
for not pursuing Robert after the battle.

00:01:43.854 --> 00:01:47.607
We had cut him off from the Stormlands,
the seat of his power,

00:01:47.774 --> 00:01:49.400
and he had fled north,

00:01:49.526 --> 00:01:54.905
within easy grasp of Lord Tywin Lannister,
the Hand ofAerys for 20 years.

00:01:55.282 --> 00:01:59.577
My father moved instead to lay siege
to Robert's ancestral stronghold

00:01:59.745 --> 00:02:01.245
of Storm's End.

00:02:01.371 --> 00:02:04.999
The rose would strangle the stag,
as the lion pounced.

00:02:05.417 --> 00:02:06.959
So we waited,

00:02:07.544 --> 00:02:11.005
but the lion slumbered
and Robert slipped past the King's forces

00:02:11.089 --> 00:02:12.715
to join Ned Stark.

00:02:13.634 --> 00:02:16.802
We could have lifted the siege
and deployed our armies north

00:02:16.887 --> 00:02:18.554
to aid the crown.

00:02:18.722 --> 00:02:23.726
We could have stormed the walls of the castle
and made Robert homeless,

00:02:24.269 --> 00:02:28.648
but we had ample supplies,
control of land and sea,

00:02:28.732 --> 00:02:31.484
and, most of all, patience.

00:02:32.986 --> 00:02:36.530
Our siege would succeed, eventually,

00:02:36.907 --> 00:02:39.617
at little cost of life to us.

00:02:40.911 --> 00:02:43.996
lf Robert prolonged the war
with minor victories,

00:02:44.081 --> 00:02:47.792
our capture of Storm's End
would hasten his downfall.

00:02:48.585 --> 00:02:50.544
And if Robert won the war,

00:02:50.629 --> 00:02:54.632
well, it would not do
for him to find us in his halls

00:02:54.716 --> 00:02:57.968
with the bodies of his brother Stannis
and his sworn men.

00:02:58.053 --> 00:03:03.766
When the lion finally showed his colors
and purged King's Landing,

00:03:04.226 --> 00:03:06.644
we knew our cause was lost.

00:03:07.145 --> 00:03:11.065
My father chose the peaceful route
and bent the knee to Robert,

00:03:11.149 --> 00:03:13.150
who heartily pardoned us.

00:03:14.069 --> 00:03:19.615
Strange, considering how we'd beaten him
and starved his brother to the brink of death.

00:03:20.492 --> 00:03:23.953
We were to keep our lands, castle and title.

00:03:24.287 --> 00:03:27.623
But we knew that
we would never be welcome at court.

00:03:28.083 --> 00:03:29.750
lt didn't matter.

00:03:30.127 --> 00:03:33.379
The Reach was still the most fertile
of the Seven Kingdoms

00:03:33.463 --> 00:03:35.506
and under our hand.

00:03:36.633 --> 00:03:40.052
Every flower, even the rose, needs pruning.

00:03:41.805 --> 00:03:43.639
Then it grows strong.

